@group
    @title=XMLDOC template
    @brief=The section describes the template that creates XML doc file from the documentation for a C# project.
    @ingroup=templates
    @key=xmldocTemplate

    The null template is located in 
    `%docgen%/template/xmldoc/main.xls` 

    The following parameters may be specified for the template

    @table
        @row
            @header=yes
            @col
                @width=30%
                Parameter
            @end
            @col
                Description
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `assembly`
            @end
            @col
                The name of the assembly (without `.dll` extension)
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `namespace`
            @end
            @col
                A regular expression for namespace(s) to include
                into the XMLDoc (useful if documentation 
                covers multiple assemblies). 
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `write-summary`
            @end
            @col
                `yes` or `no`

                The parameter defines whether only
                the content of brief tag or the whole
                summary needs to be saved for classes and methods.

                In case your documentation has rich formatting 
                in detailed description (e.g. a lot of tables, lists)
                it may be not a good idea to save this
                information to XMLDoc because formatting support
                there is highly limited. 
            @end
        @end
    @end
@end
